  "question": {
    "text": "A body is moved along a straight line by a machine delivering a constant power. The distance moved by the body in time ' $t$ ' is proportional to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZFpBZ",
      "text": "\n$t^{3 / 4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jmNvg",
      "text": "\n$t^{3 / 2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZTAQP",
      "text": "\n$t^{1 / 4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SwHhZ",
      "text": "\n$t^{1 / 2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Power $=$ F. V\n$\\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{m}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{dV}}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{m} \\cdot \\mathrm{v} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{dV}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=$ constant $=\\mathrm{C}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dV}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{C}}{\\mathrm{m}}=\\mathrm{k} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{vdv}=\\mathrm{kdt} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\int \\mathrm{vdv}=\\int \\mathrm{kdt} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{V}^2}{2}=\\mathrm{kt}+\\mathrm{c}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v} \\propto(\\mathrm{t})^{1 / 2}$        $\\frac{\\mathrm{ds}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\mathrm{c} \\cdot \\mathrm{t}^{1 / 2}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\int \\mathrm{ds}=\\int\\left(\\mathrm{c} \\cdot \\mathrm{t}^{1 / 2}\\right) \\mathrm{dt} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{S}=\\mathrm{C} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{t}^{3 / 2}$     $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{S}=\\frac{\\mathrm{ct}^{3 / 2}}{3 / 2} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{s} \\propto \\mathrm{t}^{3 / 2}$",
    "image": null
  },
